"Nala's quest is System Tutorial, at the Cinder Isle: survive 31 days or escape the Cinder Isle."
"Her sponsor changed the tutorial's format from Training Grounds to Survival Challenge."
"The tutorial's 31 days count from the moment Nala came to on the Black Shore, near ten on day one."
"The tutorial runs in three phases; the kiosk leaves each phase's details for her to find."
"The second phase begins at dawn on day seven, and the third at dawn on day twenty-two."
"The kiosk is a black obelisk on the Black Shore's north headland, some three miles north of her."
"Chests are hidden across the isle, graded from wood at the low end to gold at the high end."
"Every chest gives items or other prizes, and tutorial knowledge points to spend at the kiosk."
"In phase one the dangers are thirst, heat, the lowland beasts and cinderstorms."
"A cinderstorm is a squall of scalding wind and ash-thick rain the peak breathes out over the isle."
"Before a cinderstorm the sky goes copper, the birds go quiet and ash begins to sift down."
"In the open a cinderstorm burns skin and chokes breath; caves and the dungeon shelter from it."
"The first cinderstorm comes on the evening of day four and drives across the whole west coast."
"The first dungeon, the Salt Halls, opens from a sea cave under the Black Shore's south headland."
"The sea cave to the Salt Halls can be walked into only at low tide, around dawn and dusk."
"The Salt Halls are the drowned halls of a dead sea people, meant for a contestant near level five."
"The Salt Halls hold one boss, the Tidewarden, and a silver chest behind it."
"The second phase opens with the Black Shore and the low coast sinking under the sea in one night."
"In phase two the lowland forest is the edge of the land, and tuskhound packs come down to hunt it."
"The third phase opens as the sea rises into the lowland forest, driving the beasts to the highlands."
"In phase three the beasts fight for the high ground, and the sea keeps climbing toward the peak."
"When phase three begins, the way off the isle opens: a portal in the crater rim of the Smoking Peak."
"Stepping through the crater portal escapes the isle and ends Nala's tutorial."
"On the tutorial's last days a great cinderstorm, big as a sky, bears down on the peak."
"The tutorial's rewards are set at its end by how well Nala did."
